# Presentation-golden corpus manifest for Spyro 2 (fields as in
# games/spyro-1/corpus/presentation-corpus.manifest: name|start|interval|freeze|pins).
#
# attract-demo has no bk2: the row is the plain boot, the title screen and the
# attract demo, which need no input. A movie-less row takes its length from its
# last pin, so every frame it wants is pinned.
#
# The pins are the demo's level-loaded stretches, read off the native terrain
# feed's per-present triangle count over a 19010-VBL boot. The count holds at
# 1985 between segments (the title-screen world) and departs from it while a
# demo level is resident: 2731-3149, 3153-3785, 5877-7201, 9293-11111,
# 13203-14743 and 16835-17985. Each pin sits inside one of those stretches,
# clear of its load transient, so the row covers five distinct levels of world
# geometry and texture data. The grid samples between them hold the
# title-screen world.
# 3785 is a camera cut: the demo's second segment ends with the camera stepping
# 98094 world units in one tick, with every drawn record carrying a previous
# tick of its own. The intermediate leg there shows the previous tick for the
# whole interval; the canonical leg is unaffected.
# 700 and 1400 are the title screen: the logo sprite and the "press start"
# text, linked into the ordering table at an explicit depth slot
# (func_8001B354) rather than at the head (func_8001B390); pinned for the
# slotted-insert hook. Pins below start are unioned with the grid.
# 484 is the boot scene before the title: under --lod extended the distant
# low-poly spires between the left cliffs and the skull do not draw, where
# --lod original and the guest reference draw them (64533 px differ).
attract-demo|3400|3000||484,700,1400,3400,3785,6500,10200,14000,17400
#
# autumn-plains-skelos-badlands-portal-entry: a portal entry from the home
# world, the in-gameplay level change. 1150 is the portal transition, 1250 and
# 1350 the flight with the treasure tally, 1550 the flight with the level name,
# 1700 the arrival cutscene in the entered level.
# 1073, 1085, 1139 and 1201 are the transition's quiet regime edges: the ticks
# where g_GameState steps -1 -> 0 -> 1 -> 2 and 6 -> 7, each stepping the
# camera by at most 116 world units, three orders under the cut guard's
# position threshold and inside its rotation threshold. The pair across such an
# edge spans two simulation regimes rather than one motion, so the
# intermediate leg holds the previous tick instead of lerping the chord; the
# canonical leg is unaffected.
autumn-plains-skelos-badlands-portal-entry|1150|200||850,851,852,1073,1085,1139,1150,1201,1250,1350,1550,1700
#
# colossus-ice-skating: the player on the Colossus rink with the mirrored copy
# under the ice. 921, 1121 and 1161 are intermediate legs whose tick pair spans a
# body keyframe advance; 1123 is the leg after one.
colossus-ice-skating|900|200||921,930,1121,1123,1161

# summer-forest-collect-orb: the orb pickup with the 3D orb HUD icon at the
# bottom edge. 882 is the reported tick where the guest frames the orb icon
# with four golden facets and the native draws the orb alone; 870 and 894
# bracket it. The bk2 is 884 frames, so the grid stops at 886.
summer-forest-collect-orb|882|2||870,882,894
#
# shady-oasis-flame: two flame breaths in Shady Oasis. The flame's primitives
# are written at VBL 842-858 (peak 846) and 960-976 (peak 964); 848 is an
# intermediate leg inside the first breath.
shady-oasis-flame|840|200||846,848,850,964
#
# open-pause-menu: the pause menu open over Summer Forest, 900 and 918. The
# menu box is an opaque flat quad under ten tiled panels, a frame and six
# rows of sprite text; the guidebook page beside it carries quad-form glyphs
# (the level banner, the two gem-row slashes).
open-pause-menu|900|200||900,918
#
# open-guidebook: the guidebook open on its contents page, 980 and 998. The
# right-hand column (entry names, placeholder dashes, per-cent signs) is
# quad-form glyph text; the digits are sprite text.
open-guidebook|960|200||980,998
#
# glimmer-pogo-dialogue: the first dialogue in Glimmer. At 1000 the large
# semi-transparent text box and the speaker's name box are both open; the
# large box's four corners are the stepped corner pieces. 700 is the title
# fly-in before the level, where the game's logo slides in at the top.
# 897, 901 and 903 straddle Pogo's blend from anim 0 into anim 3 (the id
# changes at 903); 987 and 989 straddle two NPCs' blend from anim 0 into
# anim 1: the intermediate legs show whether the sub-tick pose is continuous
# across a tick while the game blends toward the next animation.
glimmer-pogo-dialogue|900|200||700,897,901,903,987,989,1000
# Pause menu mid-level: the framebuffer window copies draw buffer 0 at VBL
# 1469 and shrinks over 1454-1469 from full screen to the lower-left
# quarter; pins at the first full-window frame, mid-shrink and settled.
# Synthesized: idle to 1450 then Start (make_bk2.py --hold 1450:1460:Start).
pause-menu-midlevel|1440|200||1454,1462,1500
#
# start-new-game: same-moby self-interpenetration. Two faces of one
# moby that cross in 3D show their crossing contour under true depth, where
# the PSX paints each face whole in OT order; the same-moby rank applies the
# game's paint order between such faces only. At 92 a pink sliver shows
# through a near dark shape. Start 470 (the movie is 473 VBLs) keeps the grid
# to two samples.
start-new-game|470|10||92
# intro cutscene, VBL 1094: one of the sheep's eyes is covered by its own
# face geometry (native); the guest draws the eye.
intro-sheep-eye|1084|10||1094|--skip-to-cutscene intro
# intro cutscene, VBL 1597-1605 at 16:9: on intermediate presents the static
# tree moby on the left leaves the screen and returns.
intro-tree-subtick|1597|2||1597,1599,1600,1601,1602,1603,1605|--skip-to-cutscene intro
# intro_arrival cutscene, VBL 1130-1146: a face of the left green wall gem
# flickers as the camera moves, the gem and the wall it is set into trading
# visibility at the gem's outline (native); the guest's outline is steady.
intro-arrival-gem|1128|2||1136,1137,1138,1139,1140|--skip-to-cutscene intro_arrival
# intro_arrival cutscene, VBL 1410-1416: the base of the portal moby slides
# against the ground terrain from tick to tick (native).
intro-arrival-portal-base|1406|2||1410,1411,1412,1413,1414,1415,1416|--skip-to-cutscene intro_arrival
# intro cutscene at 32:9, VBL 1022-1026: two terrain faces at the far right
# of the frame do not draw (native).
intro-32x9-farright|1018|2||1022,1024,1026|--skip-to-cutscene intro --aspect 32:9
# intro_arrival cutscene, VBL 5256-5260: the roof of Ripto's mouth speckles
# dark through its red face (native); the guest draws it clean.
intro-arrival-ripto-mouth|5250|2||5256,5258,5260|--skip-to-cutscene intro_arrival
# crush_intro cutscene, VBL 1012: orb geometry stretches across the screen
# on the sub-tick view (native); the canonical tick draws clean.
crush-intro-orb-stretch|1004|2||1010,1011,1012,1013,1014|--skip-to-cutscene crush_intro
# crush_intro cutscene, VBL 1603: on a camera cut the mobys vanish for a
# moment on the sub-tick view (native); the canonical ticks draw them.
crush-intro-cut-mobys|1597|2||1601,1602,1603,1604,1605|--skip-to-cutscene crush_intro
# attract-demo-spawn-jump: a class 0x1e3 moby placed without a marker the
# native path reads (named residual); the sub-tick view lerps across it.
# Blessed pre-fix.
attract-demo-spawn-jump|14039|2||14041,14042,14043,14044,14045
# glimmer-32x9-leftedge: the reported free-camera pose at 32:9; the terrain
# occlusion cull's frustum half bounded each sector's sphere with a square
# box too small off-axis and culled sector 69 at the left edge (pink
# background). Blessed on the headless-occlusion build, before the fix.
glimmer-32x9-leftedge|1898|2||1900|--skip-to-level glimmer --aspect 32:9 OPENPETE_FREECAM_POSE=30338,87973,7965,-194,52
